      "evidence": "`def-radical-extension` allows any step with `F_i=F_{i-1}(\\alpha_i)` and `\\alpha_i^{m_i}=a_i`, with no nonzero hypothesis on `\\alpha_i` or `a_i`. But the cited dependency `prop-splitting-field-of-x-n-minus-a` says: `Suppose an extension E/F contains a nonzero root \\alpha of x^n-a.` In step 1.2 the proof applies [L1] to the last radical step without excluding `\\alpha=0`. A valid witness tower can have a trivial zero step, e.g. `F=F_0\\subseteq F_1=F` with `\\alpha=0`, `m=2`, `a=0`; then the proposition's hypothesis fails, so the citation drops a required condition.",
